        {
          "id": "c5ed56fe-0208-3e66-8899-b3a55ea7cb3e",
          "content": {
            "id": "c5ed56fe-0208-3e66-8899-b3a55ea7cb3e",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Camden National (CAC): Margin Contraction Challenges Bullish Growth Narrative Despite Strong Earnings Outlook",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Camden National (CAC) posted a net profit margin of 26.6% this quarter, slightly down from last year\u2019s 27.7%. Earnings growth surged 22.3% over the year, which is well above its recent five-year annual decline of 7.5%. Looking ahead, analysts forecast robust annual earnings growth of 25.7% and revenue advancing 11.6%, both outpacing the broader US market. Shares currently trade at $38.81, below an internal fair value estimate of $63.20. With high-quality earnings and no shareholder dilution,...",
